-- A record field's default may not read a section input
-- (`typically-default-reads-input.l4`). The field's default is looked up in the
-- section the record is declared in, so that holds when a definition at the top of
-- the file has the same spelling as the section's input: `alpha` there is the
-- input, and the default is refused. It used to pass over the input for the
-- definition and give 70, with no error (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7, §4.3,
-- silent review S2).

GIVETH A NUMBER
alpha MEANS 7

§ `S`
    GIVEN alpha IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

    -- ERROR: reads the section input `alpha`
    DECLARE Config HAS
      timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (alpha TIMES 10)
      retries IS A NUMBER

    -- The same default on a rule's input is refused the same way
    GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
          k IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (alpha TIMES 10)
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    f MEANS n PLUS k
